# Speak Coach — Environment Variables

## Web (`apps/web/.env.local`)

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8787
```

Auth is email OTP + HttpOnly JWT cookies. Do not put API secrets in the web bundle.

## API (`workers/api`)

1. Copy Wrangler config (keeps account / D1 IDs off GitHub):

```bash
cp workers/api/wrangler.jsonc.example workers/api/wrangler.jsonc
# Then set database_id from: npx wrangler d1 create speak-coach
```

| Setting | Where to set |
|---------|----------------|
| Cloudflare account | `npx wrangler login` (or `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`) |
| D1 database name | `speak-coach` in `wrangler.jsonc` |
| D1 database ID | your ID from `wrangler d1 create` / dashboard |

Set secrets via Wrangler (not committed to git):

```bash
cd workers/api
npx wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET
# Optional — Resend for OTP / weekly emails
# npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY
# npx wrangler secret put EMAIL_FROM
# Optional — Cloudflare Turnstile
# npx wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY
# Optional — Expo server push in production
npx wrangler secret put EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN    # optional, for mobile server push
npx wrangler secret put VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY       # optional, for web push
npx wrangler secret put VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
```

For CI smoke:full against production, the Worker should expose OTP in register responses only when needed:

```bash
npx wrangler secret put AUTH_DEV_EXPOSE_OTP
# value: true  (never enable in production unless you accept OTP leakage in JSON)
```

Local dev: copy `workers/api/.dev.vars.example` to `.dev.vars` (gitignored):

```
JWT_SECRET=dev-jwt-secret-change-me-in-production
AUTH_DEV_EXPOSE_OTP=true
```

## Mobile (`apps/mobile`)

```bash
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8787
```

Sign in via the app’s email OTP flow; no shared access code.

## Production deploy

```bash
export NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://speak-coach-api.YOUR.workers.dev
npm run deploy:all
```

Ensure `JWT_SECRET` is set on the Worker before deploy (`npx wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET`).
